+# PROG-07 Codex agent report — evaluator profiles
+
+- Worker: Codex GPT-5.6 Sol
+- Assignment: first pass
+- Branch: `codex/eval-07-profiles`
+- Worktree: `/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO-worktrees/eval-07-profiles/DebateAI-V3`
+- Commit: `a2b1f4e7f1ac11b0f90c9d3262af01b9907f41b3`
+- Comments read through: goal packet `PROG-07-codex-profiles.md`, read 2026-08-15
+- Board mutations: none, as required by the goal packet
+
+## Delivered
+
+- Deterministic profile derivation for judge bias:
+  - `bias.leniency.v1`: a judge's grade minus the same-item panel median.
+  - `bias.settlement_contradiction.v1`: thresholded judge verdict versus the latest accepted settlement outcome for the run.
+  - `bias.lineage_favoritism_residue.v1`: same-lineage mean grade minus different-lineage mean grade, emitted as `NONE` when either comparison population is absent.
+  - `bias.addon_grade_quality.v1`: the lane-06 blind add-on grade, so add-on evidence participates in bias rank rather than being silently ignored.
+- Deterministic prowess cells per exact `(provider, model_id, model_version, domain, step)` with `n`, pinned confidence intervals, source counts, derivation inputs, hashes, and `derivation_version`.
+- Append-only `profile_cell` and `rank_snapshot` persistence using the existing evaluator schema and sequence allocator; no migration was required.
+- Versioned judge and prowess rank snapshots with deterministic tie-breaking.
+- Isolated `selectJudgesByBiasRank` rank-and-select function with health, maker exclusion, seat-count, and `SELF_ROUTING_FORBIDDEN` guards.
+- Selector remains dark: zero callers in `apps/api`, `apps/runner`, `apps/scheduler`, or `apps/evaluator-worker`; no `BOUND` state or live routing integration was added.
+
+## Mandatory handoffs preserved
+
+1. **REPLACE, never pool.** Derivation first creates the as-of active observation set and removes every observation named by an eligible successor's `supersedes_observation_id`. The superseded row remains in `evaluator.observation` as audit history but is absent from every profile aggregate. A live-Postgres mixed consensus+settlement fixture proves two audit rows produce one settlement prowess sample.
+2. **Never mix superseded-row semantics.** Consensus `NODE_STRENGTH` values and settlement `EXTERNAL_ANSWER_OUTCOME` values share the input metric `prowess.outcome.v1` but land in distinct output aggregates: `prowess.consensus-strength.v1` and `prowess.settlement-outcome.v1`. They cannot be averaged into one cell.
+3. **Bias first.** The durable pipeline order is `BIAS -> JUDGE_RANK -> PROWESS -> PROWESS_RANK`. Judge-dependent JUDGING/REVIEWING prowess derivation inputs carry the producing judge's bias-rank receipt, and the repository persists bias cells and judge ranks before prowess cells.
+
+## TDD evidence
+
+- RED: `pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/evaluator-profiles.test.ts tests/architecture/evaluator-selector-unbound.test.ts`
